    "---\n",
    "## Part 1 – Review of My Own Work\n",
    "\n",
    "My module contains two functions:\n",
    "\n",
    "**download_answer_files** — downloads quiz answer files from a cloud URL and saves them locally with consistent names (e.g. answers_respondent_1.txt). If a file does not exist it prints a warning and moves on, making the function robust to missing files.\n",
    "\n",
    "**collate_answer_files** — reads each downloaded file and combines them into one file (collated_answers.txt), with each respondent's section separated by a single asterisk (*) as required."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Part 2 – Demonstrating My Code Works"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import statistics\n",
    "from data_preparation_M2 import download_answer_files, collate_answer_files\n",
    "from data_extraction_M1 import extract_answers_sequence\n",
    "\n",
    "# Download and collate files\n",
    "download_answer_files(\n",
    "    'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fc-leeds/MATH1604_2025_2026_data/main',\n",
    "    'data',\n",
    "    70\n",
    ")\n",
    "collate_answer_files('data')\n",
    "print('Download and collation complete!')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Part 3 – Pattern Investigation\n",
    "\n",
    "We investigate three questions:\n",
    "1. What is the mean and mode of answers per question?\n",
    "2. Do answers cycle in a fixed block?\n",
    "3. Is there a relationship between question number and answer?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Extract answers from all 64 respondents\n",
    "all_answers = []\n",
    "for n in range(1, 65):\n",
    "    file_path = os.path.join('data', f'answers_respondent_{n}.txt')\n",
    "    if os.path.exists(file_path):\n",
    "        all_answers.append(extract_answers_sequence(file_path))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Respondents loaded: {len(all_answers)}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Calculate mean and mode per question\n",
    "means = []\n",
    "modes = []\n",
    "for q in range(100):\n",
    "    answers_for_q = [all_answers[r][q] for r in range(len(all_answers)) if all_answers[r][q] != 0]\n",
    "    means.append(round(statistics.mean(answers_for_q), 2))\n",
    "    modes.append(statistics.mode(answers_for_q))\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Mean per question (first 10):', means[:10])\n",
    "print('Mode per question (first 10):', modes[:10])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot mean and mode\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(14, 4))\n",
    "plt.plot(range(1, 101), means, label='Mean')\n",
    "plt.plot(range(1, 101), modes, label='Mode')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Question Number')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Answer Value')\n",
    "plt.title('Mean and Mode of Answers per Question')\n",
    "plt.legend()\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Check if answers cycle in a fixed block\n",
    "# Look at the mode sequence and check for repeating blocks\n",
    "print('Full mode sequence:')\n",
    "print(modes)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot mode sequence as scatter to spot cycling\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(14, 4))\n",
    "plt.scatter(range(1, 101), modes, c=modes, cmap='tab10', s=50)\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Question Number')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Mode Answer')\n",
    "plt.title('Mode Answer per Question - Checking for Cycling Pattern')\n",
    "plt.yticks([1, 2, 3, 4])\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Check relationship between question number and answer\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(14, 4))\n",
    "plt.scatter(range(1, 101), means, color='steelblue', s=50)\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Question Number')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Mean Answer')\n",
    "plt.title('Relationship Between Question Number and Mean Answer')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
